# Published API prices, for the "~$" cost estimate in the fleet header (afc-agent-info).
# These are list prices per 1,000,000 tokens in USD. They are NOT what a subscription plan charges;
# the estimate says what the conversation would cost if it were billed by the token.
#
# One model per line:
#   <match>  <input>  <cached input>  <output>  [from=YYYY-MM-DD]  [# note]
# <match> is looked for inside the model's id or name, lower case with spaces as dashes
# ("Gemini 4 Hydrogen" -> gemini-4-hydrogen). The FIRST matching line wins, so put a line with a
# from= date (a price that starts later) ABOVE the current one; it is skipped until that day.
# Output includes thinking / reasoning tokens. A model missing here simply shows no cost.
#
# Read from the providers' own pricing pages on 2026-11-13, standard paid tier:
#   Google     https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing  (now at aistudio.google.com/docs/pricing)
#   OpenAI     https://platform.openai.com/docs/pricing       (now at developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing)
#   Anthropic  https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/about-claude/pricing
# The pages were read through an automated fetch; check a number against the page before leaning on it.

# Google
gemini-4-hydrogen   1.50   0.075   7.50
gemini-4-argon      4.00   0.20   20.00   from=2026-12-01
gemini-4-argon      2.00   0.10   10.00
gemini-4-carbon     4.00   0.20   20.00   from=2026-12-01   # added 2026-11-16; the page gives Carbon the same figures as Argon
gemini-4-carbon     2.00   0.10   10.00
gemini-3.8-flash    1.50   0.15    7.50   from=2027-01-01
gemini-3.8-flash    0.75   0.075   3.75
gemini-3.1-pro      2.00   0.20   12.00   # prompts up to 200k tokens; above that the page says 4.00 / 0.40 / 18.00

